implementationPlan.description:
Edit scripts/tests/seat-registration.test.mjs only, with the Edit tool (TOOL witness). Never touch scripts/moe-agent.sh or scripts/moe-agent.ps1.
(a) Just above `const SEGMENTS = {` (:80) add:
```
// The taskless launch decision's first line, matched as a prefix, not a whole line:
// 3586957f appended `; VM_TASKLESS_SKIP=false` to the sh one, and the whole-line
// boundary then threw at import, so none of this file's cases ran.
const DECIDE = {
  sh: ['    MOE_SKIP_LAUNCH=false', '    if [ "$MOE_SKIP_LAUNCH" != true ] && { [ "$CLI_TYPE" = claude ]'],
  ps1: ['    $moeSkipLaunch = $false', '    if (-not $moeSkipLaunch -and $cliType -in'],
};
```
The start strings keep their 4-space indent and drop today's trailing \n. The end strings are byte-identical to today's.
(b) :86 becomes `    decide: between(sh, ...DECIDE.sh),` and :97 becomes `    decide: between(ps, ...DECIDE.ps1),`. No other boundary, fixture or case changes.
(c) Between the first top-level test (:203-215) and `for (const engine of ENGINES) {` (:217) add:
```
test('a statement appended to the decide start line stays in both decide slices', () => {
  for (const [label, source, [start, end], extra] of [
    ['sh', sh, DECIDE.sh, '; MOE_FIXTURE_EXTRA=1'],
    ['ps1', ps, DECIDE.ps1, '; $moeFixtureExtra = 1'],
  ]) {
    assert.equal(count(source, start), 1, `${label}: one decide start line`);
    const eol = source.indexOf('\n', source.indexOf(start));
    const appended = source.slice(0, eol) + extra + source.slice(eol);
    assert.equal(between(appended, start, end), between(source, start, end).replace('\n', `${extra}\n`), label);
  }
});
```
Why: count === 1 pins 'first occurrence = the decide line', which a prefix needs more than a whole line did. The equality shows the slice still starts on that line, keeps the appended statement and ends at the same end boundary (DoD 2). It is load-bearing: with \n restored on the ps1 start this case fails 'missing boundaries', and with it restored on the sh start the import throws (the architect checked both in scratch). The sh fixture now also runs `VM_TASKLESS_SKIP=false`, so the outcome slice's `[ "$VM_TASKLESS_SKIP" = true ]` branch reads false and every expected reason line stays the same. Error handling is unchanged: between() keeps its assert, so any boundary that goes missing again still fails loudly at import with the boundary named.
After editing, print `git diff -U0 -- scripts/tests/seat-registration.test.mjs` (mem:gotcha-edit-tool-trims-trailing-space). Quick loop from the worktree root (it writes only mkdtemp dirs; the PS 7 rows skip without pwsh, which is fine here): `env $(compgen -e | grep '^MOE_' | sed 's/^/-u /') node --test scripts/tests/seat-registration.test.mjs`.
